how many really expected it would end  like this for all the smiles and the  cheers in a hotel ballroom Hillary  Clinton contemplating the end of a  political career  last night I congratulated Donald Trump  and offered to work with him on behalf  of our country I hope that he will be a  successful president for all Americans  this is not the outcome we wanted or we  worked so hard for and I'm sorry that we  did not win this election for the values  we share and the vision we hold for our  country  but I feel I feel pride and gratitude  for this wonderful campaign that we  built together this vast diverse  creative unruly energized campaign you  represent the best of America and being  your candidate has been one of the  greatest honors of my life this  but please never stop believing that  fighting for what's right is worth it  and I still believe as deeply as I ever  have that if we stand together and work  together with respect for our  differences strength in our convictions  and love for this nation our best days  are still I have a class it took just a  few hours last night for expectant  optimism to turn to shattering disbelief  they'd been ready for America's first  woman president but left with their  worlds turned upside down like many  those who shaped Clinton's political  career are wondering how and why she  always wanted to change things for the  better if she wanted to get people  brought her health care she wanted to  help fix the economy I I think she had a  tremendous amount of heart and always  thought she'd be an excellent president  from the moment she launched her  campaign some saw the presidency as her  destiny but polls never showed a big  lead and whatever the dysfunction on the  other side many Americans feel she faced  a bigger challenge she's a very powerful  very successful woman she's a great  politician which doesn't make her maybe  the greatest person ever but I think  she's a she would be a much better  president than Trump I think 